\title{Parquet Store}
\description{
S4 Class extending \link[=fileStore-class]{fileStore} for indexed storage of tabular data
in Apache Parquet format. \code{parquetStores} provide delayed/query-based
access to data rather than loading into memory. They are not intended for
in-place updates or edits. Create with \code{\link[=parquetStore]{parquetStore()}}.

Stores represent a query interface to on-disk data and do not contain the
actual table data as state.

\verb{[, j]} indexing is supported. \verb{[i, ]} row indexing is not -- use
filter/crop-based access instead.

\code{nrow()} and \code{dim()} calls return as \code{numeric} instead of \code{integer} to
support row counts exceeding R's int32 limit (~2.1 billion).
}
